count, CPython's messages."] [1442 1 "// ---- object's pickling protocol (typeobject.c's object___reduce_ex__, reduce_newobj, object_getstate) ----"] [1444 1 "// importModule is __import__(name) through the interpreter's builtins (PY5e's import system)."] [1453 1 "// importErrorType is ImportError when the runtime has it, else RuntimeError."] [1469 1 "// objectGetState is object.__getstate__: the instance's __dict__ (None when empty), with its"] [1470 1 "// __slots__' values as a second dictionary."] [1489 3 "// the basic size's check: a built-in base's fields, or slots the names do not cover, cannot be saved"] [1523 1 "// typeSlotNames is _PyType_GetSlotNames: the class's __slotnames__, else copyreg._slotnames's answer; nil for none."] [1584 2 "// reduce_newobj: a state is required of what its arguments, items and pairs do not rebuild"] [1607 1 "// selfMethod puts a built-in method that takes a subclass's instance itself in t's dictionary."] [1613 2 "// object_getstate: object's own __getstate__ with the required check, any other called"] [1622 2 "// set_reduce, deque_reduce, bytearray's _common_reduce: type(self), its items, the state"] [1659 2 "// method_reduce: getattr(self, name)"] [1668 2 "// object___sizeof__: tp_basicsize, here the header's two words"] [1679 3 "// typeobject.c's object___reduce_ex___impl: a __reduce__ overriding object's, a built-in type's too"] [1708 1 "// BuiltinValue is the built-in value an instance of a class deriving from a built-in type carries"] [1709 1 "// (a list subclass's list), else o itself: for the core types' functions taking their subclasses."] [1712 1 "// builtinHasDict is a built-in type's tp_dictoffset: it, or a built-in type it derives from, shows a __dict__."] [1722 1 "// builtinHasWeak is a built-in type's tp_weaklistoffset, for the types one can derive from."] [1733 1 "// varSized is a type's tp_itemsize: its instances hold their items after the header, so that a class deriving"] [1734 1 "// from it can add no __slots